1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,656
If I lost everything tomorrow

2
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:04,737
and had to start investing

3
00:00:04,757 --> 00:00:06,754
from zero dollars in 2026,

4
00:00:06,774 --> 00:00:08,444
here's exactly what I'd

5
00:00:08,464 --> 00:00:09,085
do.

6
00:00:09,105 --> 00:00:10,198
Not stock tips.

7
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:11,003
Not crypto.

8
00:00:11,023 --> 00:00:12,797
Just the order of steps

9
00:00:12,817 --> 00:00:14,600
that actually works.

10
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:15,783
Get the order wrong,

11
00:00:15,803 --> 00:00:17,312
and you can do everything

12
00:00:17,332 --> 00:00:19,418
right and still end up broke.

13
00:00:19,438 --> 00:00:20,336
Seven steps.

14
00:00:20,356 --> 00:00:21,373
Let's go.

15
00:00:21,393 --> 00:00:21,939
Step one:

16
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:23,349
find your number.

17
00:00:23,369 --> 00:00:25,017
Before you invest a single

18
00:00:25,037 --> 00:00:25,434
dollar,

19
00:00:25,454 --> 00:00:27,101
you need to know how much

20
00:00:27,121 --> 00:00:28,665
money is left after your

21
00:00:28,685 --> 00:00:29,410
bills.

22
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:31,565
Track every dollar for thirty

23
00:00:31,585 --> 00:00:31,935
days.

24
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:32,304
Rent,

25
00:00:32,324 --> 00:00:32,674
food,

26
00:00:32,694 --> 00:00:33,597
subscriptions,

27
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:34,716
everything.

28
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:36,564
Most people find a few hundred

29
00:00:36,584 --> 00:00:38,161
dollars a month they didn't

30
00:00:38,181 --> 00:00:39,840
know they were losing.

31
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,441
That gap between what you

32
00:00:41,461 --> 00:00:42,940
earn and what you spend

33
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,818
is your investing engine.

34
00:00:44,838 --> 00:00:46,083
And here's the trick:

35
00:00:46,103 --> 00:00:47,243
pay yourself first.

36
00:00:47,263 --> 00:00:49,141
Move that money out on payday,

37
00:00:49,161 --> 00:00:51,050
before you can spend it.

38
00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:53,086
A common target is to invest

39
00:00:53,106 --> 00:00:54,715
fifteen percent of your

40
00:00:54,735 --> 00:00:55,180
income.

41
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,867
If that feels impossible,

42
00:00:56,887 --> 00:00:58,728
start with one percent and

43
00:00:58,748 --> 00:01:00,912
raise it every few months.

44
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:01,516
Step two:

45
00:01:01,536 --> 00:01:03,221
build a safety net before

46
00:01:03,241 --> 00:01:04,315
you invest.

47
00:01:04,335 --> 00:01:06,163
Aim for three to six months

48
00:01:06,183 --> 00:01:07,903
of expenses in a high-yield

49
00:01:07,923 --> 00:01:09,261
savings account.

50
00:01:09,281 --> 00:01:09,588
Why?

51
00:01:09,608 --> 00:01:11,154
Because life happens.

52
00:01:11,174 --> 00:01:12,590
A car breaks down.

53
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:14,275
A job disappears.

54
00:01:14,295 --> 00:01:15,347
Without a cushion,

55
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:16,776
you'd be forced to sell

56
00:01:16,796 --> 00:01:18,205
your investments at the

57
00:01:18,225 --> 00:01:19,860
worst possible moment.

58
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,754
Keep this money boring and

59
00:01:21,774 --> 00:01:22,760
easy to reach.

60
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:24,298
It's not an investment.

61
00:01:24,318 --> 00:01:25,625
It's insurance.

62
00:01:25,645 --> 00:01:26,481
Start small.

63
00:01:26,501 --> 00:01:28,439
Even one month of expenses

64
00:01:28,459 --> 00:01:30,104
changes everything.

65
00:01:30,124 --> 00:01:30,771
Step three:

66
00:01:30,791 --> 00:01:32,486
kill high-interest debt.

67
00:01:32,506 --> 00:01:34,238
The average credit card

68
00:01:34,258 --> 00:01:36,054
in America charges about

69
00:01:36,074 --> 00:01:37,931
twenty-one percent interest

70
00:01:37,951 --> 00:01:38,875
a year.

71
00:01:38,895 --> 00:01:40,818
No investment reliably beats

72
00:01:40,838 --> 00:01:41,552
that.

73
00:01:41,572 --> 00:01:43,185
So every dollar you use

74
00:01:43,205 --> 00:01:44,931
to pay off a credit card

75
00:01:44,951 --> 00:01:47,071
earns you a guaranteed twenty-one

76
00:01:47,091 --> 00:01:47,958
percent.

77
00:01:47,978 --> 00:01:49,870
Pay the minimum on everything,

78
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:51,783
then throw every extra dollar

79
00:01:51,803 --> 00:01:53,313
at the highest interest

80
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,403
rate first.

81
00:01:54,423 --> 00:01:55,296
Mathematically,

82
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:57,192
the highest rate first saves

83
00:01:57,212 --> 00:01:58,576
the most money.

84
00:01:58,596 --> 00:02:00,405
But if you need quick wins

85
00:02:00,425 --> 00:02:01,569
to stay motivated,

86
00:02:01,589 --> 00:02:03,120
paying off the smallest

87
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,672
balance first works too.

88
00:02:04,692 --> 00:02:06,390
The best plan is the one

89
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:07,767
you stick with.

90
00:02:07,787 --> 00:02:08,384
Step four:

91
00:02:08,404 --> 00:02:09,999
grab the free money.

92
00:02:10,019 --> 00:02:12,014
If your job offers a 401(k)

93
00:02:12,034 --> 00:02:12,455
match,

94
00:02:12,475 --> 00:02:14,407
contribute at least enough

95
00:02:14,427 --> 00:02:16,488
to get the full match.

96
00:02:16,508 --> 00:02:18,321
Say you earn sixty thousand

97
00:02:18,341 --> 00:02:18,821
dollars,

98
00:02:18,841 --> 00:02:20,098
put in six percent,

99
00:02:20,118 --> 00:02:21,765
and your employer matches

100
00:02:21,785 --> 00:02:23,033
half of that.

101
00:02:23,053 --> 00:02:24,513
That's an extra eighteen

102
00:02:24,533 --> 00:02:25,941
hundred dollars a year,

103
00:02:25,961 --> 00:02:27,589
just for showing up.

104
00:02:27,609 --> 00:02:29,409
It's an instant fifty percent

105
00:02:29,429 --> 00:02:30,960
return before the market

106
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:31,817
does anything.

107
00:02:31,837 --> 00:02:34,016
Never leave it on the table.

108
00:02:34,036 --> 00:02:34,994
Step five:

109
00:02:35,014 --> 00:02:37,004
open a Roth IRA.

110
00:02:37,024 --> 00:02:37,587
In 2026,

111
00:02:37,607 --> 00:02:39,567
you can put in up to seven

112
00:02:39,587 --> 00:02:41,547
thousand five hundred dollars

113
00:02:41,567 --> 00:02:42,451
a year.

114
00:02:42,471 --> 00:02:44,100
You pay tax on the money

115
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:44,366
now,

116
00:02:44,386 --> 00:02:45,695
but it grows tax-free,

117
00:02:45,715 --> 00:02:47,344
and in retirement you can

118
00:02:47,364 --> 00:02:49,001
take it out tax-free.

119
00:02:49,021 --> 00:02:50,880
For most young people starting

120
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:51,506
from zero,

121
00:02:51,526 --> 00:02:53,281
that's one of the best deals

122
00:02:53,301 --> 00:02:54,705
in the tax code.

123
00:02:54,725 --> 00:02:56,189
There are income limits,

124
00:02:56,209 --> 00:02:57,832
so check that you qualify

125
00:02:57,852 --> 00:02:59,537
before you contribute.

126
00:02:59,557 --> 00:03:01,497
And if your income is too

127
00:03:01,517 --> 00:03:01,864
high,

128
00:03:01,884 --> 00:03:03,824
or you'd rather take a tax

129
00:03:03,844 --> 00:03:04,682
break today,

130
00:03:04,702 --> 00:03:06,519
a traditional IRA is the

131
00:03:06,539 --> 00:03:07,818
other option.

132
00:03:07,838 --> 00:03:08,421
Step six:

133
00:03:08,441 --> 00:03:10,444
what do you actually buy?

134
00:03:10,464 --> 00:03:11,703
Not one hot stock.

135
00:03:11,723 --> 00:03:13,513
Buy the whole market.

136
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:15,284
A low-cost index fund owns

137
00:03:15,304 --> 00:03:17,055
hundreds or even thousands

138
00:03:17,075 --> 00:03:19,206
of companies in one click.

139
00:03:19,226 --> 00:03:20,628
When one company fails,

140
00:03:20,648 --> 00:03:21,734
you barely notice.

141
00:03:21,754 --> 00:03:23,156
When the economy grows,

142
00:03:23,176 --> 00:03:24,642
you grow with it.

143
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,035
Look for low fees.

144
00:03:26,055 --> 00:03:27,871
The expense ratio should

145
00:03:27,891 --> 00:03:28,504
be tiny,

146
00:03:28,524 --> 00:03:30,847
a fraction of one percent.

147
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:32,771
If you want it even simpler,

148
00:03:32,791 --> 00:03:34,355
a target-date fund picks

149
00:03:34,375 --> 00:03:36,279
the mix for you and adjusts

150
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,848
as you get older.

151
00:03:37,868 --> 00:03:39,553
Index funds aren't exciting.

152
00:03:39,573 --> 00:03:40,598
That's the point.

153
00:03:40,618 --> 00:03:42,358
Instead of hunting for the

154
00:03:42,378 --> 00:03:42,798
needle,

155
00:03:42,818 --> 00:03:44,938
you buy the whole haystack.

156
00:03:44,958 --> 00:03:45,560
Step seven:

157
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,230
automate it,

158
00:03:46,250 --> 00:03:47,998
and then leave it alone.

159
00:03:48,018 --> 00:03:50,051
Set up an automatic transfer

160
00:03:50,071 --> 00:03:50,957
every payday,

161
00:03:50,977 --> 00:03:52,950
so investing happens without

162
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:53,995
willpower.

163
00:03:54,015 --> 00:03:55,597
Say you invest five hundred

164
00:03:55,617 --> 00:03:56,899
dollars a month.

165
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:58,029
After ten years,

166
00:03:58,049 --> 00:03:59,991
you've put in sixty thousand.

167
00:04:00,011 --> 00:04:01,894
At an eight percent yearly

168
00:04:01,914 --> 00:04:02,369
return,

169
00:04:02,389 --> 00:04:04,094
it could be worth about

170
00:04:04,114 --> 00:04:05,722
ninety-two thousand.

171
00:04:05,742 --> 00:04:07,028
After twenty years,

172
00:04:07,048 --> 00:04:08,927
about two hundred ninety-six

173
00:04:08,947 --> 00:04:09,900
thousand.

174
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,433
And after thirty years,

175
00:04:11,453 --> 00:04:13,137
about seven hundred fifty

176
00:04:13,157 --> 00:04:14,216
thousand dollars,

177
00:04:14,236 --> 00:04:16,147
from just one hundred eighty

178
00:04:16,167 --> 00:04:18,344
thousand of your own money.

179
00:04:18,364 --> 00:04:19,525
That's compounding.

180
00:04:19,545 --> 00:04:21,356
Your returns start earning

181
00:04:21,376 --> 00:04:22,976
their own returns.

182
00:04:22,996 --> 00:04:25,043
Eight percent is an assumption,

183
00:04:25,063 --> 00:04:26,019
not a promise.

184
00:04:26,039 --> 00:04:27,971
Real returns go up and down,

185
00:04:27,991 --> 00:04:30,246
and some years are negative.

186
00:04:30,266 --> 00:04:31,868
But time in the market is

187
00:04:31,888 --> 00:04:33,491
the one advantage you can't

188
00:04:33,511 --> 00:04:34,479
buy later.

189
00:04:34,499 --> 00:04:36,173
But what if the market crashes

190
00:04:36,193 --> 00:04:37,743
right after you start?

191
00:04:37,763 --> 00:04:39,638
It will crash at some point.

192
00:04:39,658 --> 00:04:41,589
Almost every long-term investor

193
00:04:41,609 --> 00:04:43,363
lives through several.

194
00:04:43,383 --> 00:04:44,987
When you invest the same

195
00:04:45,007 --> 00:04:46,178
amount every month,

196
00:04:46,198 --> 00:04:47,801
a crash means your money

197
00:04:47,821 --> 00:04:49,479
buys more shares at lower

198
00:04:49,499 --> 00:04:50,292
prices.

199
00:04:50,312 --> 00:04:51,875
That's called dollar-cost

200
00:04:51,895 --> 00:04:52,520
averaging,

201
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,280
and it turns scary drops

202
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,422
into sales.

203
00:04:55,442 --> 00:04:56,990
The real danger isn't the

204
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:57,355
crash.

205
00:04:57,375 --> 00:04:58,923
It's panicking and selling

206
00:04:58,943 --> 00:05:00,191
at the bottom.

207
00:05:00,211 --> 00:05:00,436
Now,

208
00:05:00,456 --> 00:05:02,040
what would I not do?

209
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,795
I would not day trade.

210
00:05:03,815 --> 00:05:05,451
A study of Brazilian day

211
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,383
traders found that ninety-seven

212
00:05:07,403 --> 00:05:09,094
percent of those who kept

213
00:05:09,114 --> 00:05:10,695
at it for three hundred

214
00:05:10,715 --> 00:05:12,124
days lost money.

215
00:05:12,144 --> 00:05:14,097
I would not chase meme coins

216
00:05:14,117 --> 00:05:15,900
or hot tips from strangers

217
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,731
online.

218
00:05:16,751 --> 00:05:18,306
And I would not wait for

219
00:05:18,326 --> 00:05:19,423
the perfect moment.

220
00:05:19,443 --> 00:05:20,717
It never comes.

221
00:05:20,737 --> 00:05:22,594
So here's the whole plan.

222
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:23,875
Find your number.

223
00:05:23,895 --> 00:05:25,348
Build a safety net.

224
00:05:25,368 --> 00:05:27,014
Kill high-interest debt.

225
00:05:27,034 --> 00:05:28,551
Grab the free match.

226
00:05:28,571 --> 00:05:29,832
Open a Roth IRA.

227
00:05:29,852 --> 00:05:31,433
Buy the whole market.

228
00:05:31,453 --> 00:05:32,330
Automate it,

229
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:33,415
and wait.

230
00:05:33,435 --> 00:05:33,922
Boring?

231
00:05:33,942 --> 00:05:34,238
Yes.

232
00:05:34,258 --> 00:05:36,520
But boring is how real wealth

233
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,168
is usually built.

234
00:05:38,188 --> 00:05:39,748
Which step are you on right

235
00:05:39,768 --> 00:05:39,981
now?

236
00:05:40,001 --> 00:05:41,709
Tell me in the comments.

237
00:05:41,729 --> 00:05:43,891
This video is for education

238
00:05:43,911 --> 00:05:44,288
only.

239
00:05:44,308 --> 00:05:46,984
It's not financial advice.
